{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1383620-akaname-yokai","id":1383620,"title":"Akaname Yokai","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-24T10:06:41-07:00","id":1383620,"title":"Akaname Yokai","content":"<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This is part of a series I have been tinkering with based around Japanese Yokai. As I feel that these supernatural beings are better depicted as creatures of the Dreaming than the Hsien, I thought I would make some Changeling kiths to reflect them. And as Anime has brought so many wonderful stories to the hearts and dreams of Western folk, I think they would make for a wonderful addition to Changeling. More yokai, and other beings will be posted over on my <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/Aaronsmonsters\" target=\"_blank\">patreon</a>.<br /> <br /> The Akaname are a favorite of mine. They are so delightfully disgusting! And I could see them adapting to Western cities with little trouble.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Akaname</span></b> (fi<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">lth licker)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><img src=\"https://statici.behindthevoiceactors.com/behindthevoiceactors/_img/chars/mame-a-letter-to-momo-75.5.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Akaname is a Yokai kith born of the dread of filthy bathrooms, bad smells and dirty people. As such their fae mein appears as small, goblin-like Yokai with bulging eyes and lolling, overlong tongues. Like cockroaches, rats, lice, and other pests, Akaname detest clean, well-kept homes, and only appear where the owners show a complete lack of sanitary discipline. Within fae society, the Akaname are bottom dwellers, and are often hated and reviled because of their habits. Despite this, they are not evil, many are intelligent and kindly, often watching out for the wretched and overlooked people and animals that dwell in harsh conditions. In mortal society, the Akaname are often found working jobs where hygiene is regularly overlooked such as sewer workers, janitors and fry cooks.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Akaname are found all over Japan, and have spread around the world. A significant number of this kith dwell in Concordia, with a preference for big, dirty cities where they might hide themselves and indulge in their sticky tastes.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Affinity:</span></b> Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Revelry:</span> </b>Akaname delight in filth, dirt and grime, taking great joy in disgusting others. They derive glamour from the revulsion others have for filthy conditions and horrible smells and tastes. They also gain glamour from sampling new and disgusting sensations such as tasting horrible food or smelling a particularly vile stink.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Unleashing:</span></b> Akaname unleashing typically comes with horrible smells, unidentifiable stains and smears. The scurrying of rats and cockroaches and the rotting of paper and wood.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Birthrights:</span></span></b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Filth Eater</b> \u2014 Akaname are immune to ingested poisons and disease, from spoiled food and poisoned drink to a septic sandwich, and adds three dice to resist the effects of supernatural toxins. This Birthright does not protect the character from alcohol, gasses or injected substances.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Night Dweller</b> \u2014 Akaname prefer their privacy while they lurk, and are experts on detecting those who would disturb them. Any attempts to sneak up on or surprise an Akaname by mundane means automatically fail. Additionally, she gains a \u20132 difficulty to see through magical means of deception.</span></span></span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Frailty:</span></span></span></span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Gross \u2014</b> All Akaname have an Appearance of 0 in their fae mien (and 1 in their mortal seeming), which can never be raised. Also, Akaname can never have a Strength rating above 3 due to their withered limbs.</span></span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 04-24-2020, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T11:11:06-07:00","id":1383631,"title":"","content":"Brilliant! Love it my man!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T08:52:57-07:00","id":1385607,"title":"","content":"Ooooh! I love the Akaname, they are so disgustingly vile and down right creepy in their stories, I'm very excited to see what other Yokai you have in store!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}